[{"author":{"id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY5MDMyMjYx","is_bot":false,"login":"mpmdw","name":""},"body":"# BINDING TEXT (Ed, 2026-09-25): A-R5b v1.1 is approved for the pre-registration\n\n**Ed's words** (interactive session 4b): \"you've the permission you requested in 1\". The request was: \"go ahead with A-R5b, add the permission rule\".\n\n**Approved:** append the amendment **A-R5b v1.1**, exactly the §5.8 text of the cold ruling `docs/process_traces/2026-09-25-activation-ed17a643/10-coldgate-packet-bfg/30-addendum/21-coldgate-fable-bfg-addendum-ruling.md` (branch `docs/2026-09-25-152c9255`), below the sealed Revision 5 text of `configs/calibration/preregistration_d079_epoch_25g83_rev1.md`, **after PR #418 merges**. Add its `docs/decision_log.md` entry as the ruling requires. The whole-file digest after the append is the one pinned in the W1 notice and arm material.\n\n**Scope:** only that file, and only that append. Any other edit to the pre-registration still needs its own approval.\n\n**Machine permission** (untracked, per-machine): `/Users/edr/code/JouleWise/.claude/settings.local.json` now allows `Edit(**/configs/calibration/preregistration_d079_epoch_25g83_rev1.md)`. It also carries one auto-mode classifier allow rule, scoped to this append and citing this directive. After the append lands and its digest is pinned, the magistrate should remove both entries. Ed approved the rule's addition; its removal restores the default.\n","number":422,"title":"Directive (Ed, 2026-09-25): A-R5b v1.1 approved — append §5.8 text to the 25G83 pre-registration after #418 merges; narrow permission rule added"},{"author":{"id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY5MDMyMjYx","is_bot":false,"login":"mpmdw","name":""},"body":"# BINDING TEXT (Ed, 2026-09-25): battery float is MANDATORY for every measurement window; anything germane to the verity of the science is mandatory\n\n**Ed's words:** \"make it binding obviously anything germane to the verity of the science is mandatory\"\n\n**1. The battery gate, for every measurement window** (W1/W2, calibration, evidence and claim-bearing windows; not only W1):\n- **At arm and immediately before publication/t0**, read `ioreg -r -c AppleSmartBattery` and require:\n  - `ExternalConnected = Yes`;\n  - `IsCharging = No`;\n  - |InstantAmperage| ≤ 200 mA (two's complement handled).\n- **Log** the raw values to the stage and the arm record.\n- **Failure postpones the arm.** It is never waived.\n- **Harvest check:** if any slot records `is_charging = true`, or its battery current exceeds the bound, the window is confounded and not used for any claim or acceptance. The arm notice and the harvest record say so.\n- **The code-level t0 gate (BATTERY-FLOAT-GATE-01)** remains a full-gate lane and should land promptly. Until it does, the procedural check above is mandatory.\n\n**2. The general principle, binding on all roles.** A check, disclosure or gate that bears on whether a measured or claimed number is TRUE is mandatory. It is not at the magistrate's discretion and not traded against schedule. Examples: instrument state, machine quietness, clock anchoring, calibration binding, contamination, and the statistical adequacy of a claim rule. Discretion applies only to things that cannot change a number (ceremony, docs, bookkeeping; see #415). When in doubt, treat the item as germane.\n\n**Context:** issue #420. Ed changed the charge setting from an 80 % cap to 100 % on 2026-09-25, and the battery charged all afternoon. Charging adds heat (SoC temperature and leakage) and invalidates wall-meter readings.\n","number":421,"title":"Directive (Ed, 2026-09-25): battery-float gate mandatory for every window; anything germane to the verity of the science is mandatory"},{"author":{"id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY5MDMyMjYx","is_bot":false,"login":"mpmdw","name":""},"body":"# BINDING TEXT (Ed, 2026-09-25): STOP asking Ed to turn off macOS automatic updates. The request is retired.\n\n**Ed's words:** \"i keep getting emailed about turning auto updates off - can you fix that persistent reminder\". Earlier the same day: \"I don't think auto updates are on or ever were on in the first place. I updated Mac OS because I didn't even think about how it might affect the instrument.\"\n\n**Verified by the agent, 2026-09-25 (interactive 4b), read-only:**\n- `/Library/Preferences/com.apple.SoftwareUpdate` has **no `AutomaticallyInstallMacOSUpdates` key**: macOS updates are **not** installed automatically.\n- Its `DoItLaterTonightAttemptsCount` history shows past \"install tonight\" offers that were deferred. The 25F84 → 25G83 change was Ed's manual update, not an automatic one.\n- Still on: `AutomaticDownload = 1` (updates download in the background, and **a download does not change the OS build**), \"Automatic checking\" on, and App Store app auto-update (`com.apple.commerce AutoUpdate = 1`). None of these changes the OS build under measurement.\n\n**What to apply:**\n1. No email, notice, arm notice, record or owner-blocker list may ask Ed to turn off automatic updates again. Remove the item from RUN_STATE's owner-blocker lists and from any notice template.\n2. The instrument's protection against a build change is **mechanical**, and needs no owner action:\n   - the calibration binds `os_build` and the powermetrics sha;\n   - the arm-time cadence probe and the build binding refuse a mismatched build.\n\n   If a build change is ever detected, report it once, as a finding, and never re-ask as a standing request.\n3. Optional, Ed's choice, never to be re-asked: turn off \"Download new updates when available\" (System Settings → General → Software Update → Automatic updates ⓘ). The only purpose would be keeping background download traffic out of windows; the quiet census already catches heavy CPU.\n","number":417,"title":"Directive (Ed, 2026-09-25): stop asking Ed to turn off auto-updates — macOS OS updates are not auto-installed (verified); request retired"},{"author":{"id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY5MDMyMjYx","is_bot":false,"login":"mpmdw","name":""},"body":"# BINDING TEXT (amended by Ed, 2026-09-25): the audit runs AFTER W1/W2 pass and BEFORE any claim-bearing run. It is NOT a W1 arm precondition.\n\n**AMENDMENT (Ed, 2026-09-25, interactive 4b): \"agreed with your proposed change of order\".**\n\nThe three-family full-system audit moves from \"before W1\" to **after W1 and W2 pass and before any claim-bearing run**:\n1. **Before W1:** no full audit. The acceptance PRs pass their normal full gates, and each arm runs its cadence probe.\n2. **After W1/W2 pass, before any claim-bearing (headline) run:** the #416 audit at the frozen head that will produce paper numbers. Its evidence includes the real W1/W2 bundles, from which the auditors independently re-derive the calibration from raw data.\n3. **If the audit finds a defect in the calibration derivation path,** W1/W2 are re-run before any headline run.\n\n**Rationale.**\n- Passing windows are internal-consistency evidence, not correctness evidence (silent-wrong paths pass by definition). So the audit remains mandatory.\n- Real bundles let the auditors check numbers, not only code.\n- Live-only defects surface in real windows.\n- The headline pipeline is not frozen yet.\n- A flawed W1/W2 costs about a day to redo; a flawed headline run costs the paper.\n\nThe trigger message becomes \"CLAIM-RUN WORK COMPLETE\" (W1/W2 issued plus the headline pipeline frozen), carrying the sha and scope. The kit (main `docs/process_traces/2026-09-24-interactive-4b/30-prearm-audit-kit-416.md`) is unchanged, except that its scope adds the W1/W2 bundles.\n\n---\n\n## Original text (superseded on placement only; scope, seats and method still apply)\n\nEd, 2026-09-25 (interactive session 4b): \"i want a full multi agent fresh audit of the whole measurement system/codebase by astra 6 xhigh, fable 5.1 xhigh, and opus 5.5 xhigh\". Clarified: \"that's meant for when all the work before launching the load bearing windows\" is done.\n\n**The ruling. A pre-arm audit gate for the first load-bearing windows (W1/W2 of the 25G83 derivation, and every later claim-bearing window).**\n1. **When.** After every pre-window change has merged (PR-L, PR-R, the sealed Revision 5, and anything else on the W1 critical path), and **before W1 is armed**.\n2. **What.** A fresh, independent audit of the whole measurement system at the exact head W1 will run: instrument adapters, calibration and issuance, the night machinery (prepare, install, t0 census, driver, harvest), reduction, analysis and claim code.\n3. **Who.** Three families, each at the highest effort available: Astra 6 at xhigh, Fable 5.1, and Opus 5.5 at xhigh. They audit independently and blind to one another. Their findings are cross-verified, and BLOCKERs get refuters from a different family.\n4. **Outcome.** W1 arms only after every verified BLOCKER is fixed (under the gates for its tier) or ruled not load-bearing by a cold gate. The audit record is linked from the W1 arm notice.\n5. **Timing is Ed's call.** The audit adds hours before W1. Ed accepts that.\n\n**Who runs it.** Interactive seat 4b, if it is alive at that point. Otherwise the magistrate runs it. The magistrate signals \"pre-window work complete\" with the frozen head.\n","number":416,"title":"Directive (Ed, 2026-09-25, amended): fresh three-family full-system audit (Astra 6 xhigh, Fable 5.1, Opus 5.5 xhigh) after W1/W2 pass and before any claim-bearing run"},{"author":{"id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY5MDMyMjYx","is_bot":false,"login":"mpmdw","name":""},"body":"Ed, 04:40 PDT 2026-09-24, verbatim: \"usage is low, but usage on this acc and codex resets in the next few hours so after that reset do whatever you can to fan out and accelerate the results\". Record: docs/process_traces/2026-09-24-interactive-02a24110/01-ed-rulings-harvest-and-reply-miss.md §10 (main bce0d7df).\n\nApply:\n1. Until the reset: lean sessions (Sol seats for execution, durable pointer commits, no usage-heavy Fable fan-out). Check the Claude usage state and `codex-usage` at each launch; treat the first launch that finds both windows fresh as the reset.\n2. From the reset: maximal fan-out under the standing authorizations (multi-Sol seats in linked worktrees, Astra 6, Opus corps, Workflow fleets) on the critical path, in parallel where there is no shared invariant: the D-184 council on #407 (A3 first model night, B1 with the KM003C, headline reshaped); A280 scored night kind; A283 decoding/runtime; A291 packer consult then implementation; E2 AP-5M council and O-21 floor text; A293 estimator; pull the Qwen3 1.7B and 8B 4-bit MLX weights.\n3. Ed has left the machine; close this issue with a comment naming what was fanned out and the first model night's arm notice.","number":408,"title":"Directive: after the Claude and Codex usage reset (next few hours from 04:40 PDT 09-24), fan out maximally to accelerate results"},{"author":{"id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY5MDMyMjYx","is_bot":false,"login":"mpmdw","name":""},"body":"Instruction from Ed, transcribed by the interactive Fable session 02a24110 (2026-09-24 ≈04:40 PDT) from Ed's email of 22:19 PDT 2026-09-23 (Gmail message `1a0d1db347b562c4`, thread `1a0d12f08db9ef04`), which activations d8cc9c0a and a65fb4fa missed. Record: `docs/process_traces/2026-09-24-interactive-02a24110/01-ed-rulings-harvest-and-reply-miss.md` (main `bf5fe420`).\n\nEd's words, verbatim:\n\n> re the 4 decisions: yeah, why not publish it?\n>\n> 2. yes if you fable, opus 5.5 and astra all agree, then go ahead i trust the council\n>\n> 3 and 4, your decisions towards the best practices are authorized, just get at least opus 5.5 and astra to rule on it, with a fable 5.1 too at the end.\n\nApply as follows (questions E1–E4 of email `1a0d069e15a52ba9`, i.e. O-20, O-17, O-19, O-18 of AP-5M draft v4):\n\n1. E2 / O-17 (adopt AP-5M): adopt when Fable 5.1, Opus 5.5 and Astra all agree on the text. Convene that three-seat council; adopt on unanimity; a split goes back to Ed with the split stated, not as a re-ask.\n2. E3 / O-19 (decoding) and E4 / O-18 (n per level): the magistrate decides toward best practice, with Opus 5.5 and Astra each ruling and a Fable 5.1 final pass at the end.\n3. E1 / O-20 (publish MATH problem text): Ed's answer reads as \"publish\". Because the recommendation was the opposite and publication is hard to reverse, commit NO problem text to any public branch until this issue carries Ed's one-word confirmation (the interactive session is asking him now); everything else proceeds.\n4. O-21 (estimate-level floor check): still Ed's; the interactive session is asking him now and will comment the answer here.\n5. Send Ed no further email that asks any of E1–E4 again. From this launch onward the relaunch prompt requires searching `from:claude2.glaring610@passmail.net is:unread` across all threads before the launch email and before every work slice.\n\nClose this issue with a comment once E2–E4 are applied and E1/O-21 answers are recorded.","number":405,"title":"Directive: Ed's 22:19 PDT 09-23 rulings on E1–E4 (missed by two activations); E1 and O-21 answers to follow here"}]
